Z||000000||Sndfr||11-24-2000||01:03 PM||||You don't even know how much I love looking at those 8 cylinder engines bulging out of those engine bays!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>But right now it's not like i have money to burn so...<P>What are some ways to get the best performance out of my 4 cylinder?  It really tries hard and is a good engine (averages 8000 miles a year).<P>------------------<BR>-matthew d.<BR>"who's yo daddy?" :cool:<P>'84 SE||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||11-24-2000||04:26 PM||||The (boring) answer:  Basic tune up.  Get everything set to factory specs, and see how you like it, before you try hopping anything up.  Make sure e-brake isn't hanging up and dragging (apparently, it happens  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">).  <P>After that, try the lower-temperature thermostat and fan switch tricks (see Ogre's articles).  Maybe K&N air filter.  Main thing is, just do stuff that's reversible, so you can go back if you don't like the outcome.<P>Don't spend too much on fancy hop-ups.    After all, someday you'll drop in a different motor, right?  Meantime, keep track of your gas mileage - you'll feel better about having a Duke  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">!||||reg||1
Z||000002||horseman||11-24-2000||10:43 PM||||A couple of areas to look at after the previously mentioned tuneup. Main performance weaknesses of the duke are the camshaft(economy profile),poor ignition timing curve, and sluggish coil(limits upper rpm response).Check fieroville for better info. re: 2.5 Duke . This list is focused more on the v-6 and v-8. Alas,I found out the hard way. These guys are right though, If you want better performance get a GT or a v-8 conversion. I personally would reccommend a firebird with a H.O. 305('87-92). Every one that I have owned handled well, was easy to maintain, and got 28-31mpg on the highway! Best daily drivers that I have owned. I always wondered what a shot of laughing gas would have done for these cars. Just one pontiac lovers opinion.<BR>Still got my '66 GTO convert. and my '79 Trans Am(400w/4spd,4wheel discs)so I think I have a GOOD idea about what PONTIAC EXCITEMENT is! For what it is worth, Charlie||||reg||14
